@startuml Document Session Workflow - Sequence Diagram

title /use-case:document-session Workflow (v3.4.0+)

actor Developer
participant "Claude Code" as Claude
participant "CLI Dispatcher" as CLI
participant "document-ai-session.sh" as DocScript
participant "Git" as Git
participant "GitHub API" as GitHub
participant "File System" as FS
participant "sync-ai-use-cases.sh" as Sync
participant "Hub Repository" as Hub

== Version Check ==
Developer -> Claude: /use-case:document-session
activate Claude
Claude -> CLI: ai-use-case version
activate CLI
CLI -> Git: Get current version
Git --> CLI: v3.9.0
CLI -> GitHub: Check latest version
GitHub --> CLI: v3.9.0
CLI --> Claude: Version up-to-date
deactivate CLI

== Session Detection (v3.4.0+) ==
Claude -> GitHub: gh pr list --state merged --limit 10
activate GitHub
GitHub --> Claude: List of recent PRs
deactivate GitHub

Claude -> Git: git log --since="7 days ago"
activate Git
Git --> Claude: Recent commits
deactivate Git

Claude -> FS: Check .usecase/cases/ for existing docs
activate FS
FS --> Claude: List of documented sessions
deactivate FS

== Interactive Session Selection ==
Claude -> Developer: Present options:\n1. PR #123: "Add feature X"\n2. Current conversation\n3. Commit abc123: "Fix bug Y"
Developer -> Claude: Select option 1 (PR #123)

== Git History Analysis (Parallel) ==
Claude -> Git: git log --since="PR merge time"
activate Git
Claude -> Git: git show --stat HEAD
Claude -> Git: git diff PR_BASE..PR_HEAD
Claude -> Git: git status --short
Git --> Claude: Commit history
Git --> Claude: File statistics
Git --> Claude: Code changes
Git --> Claude: Working tree status
deactivate Git

== Session Information Extraction ==
Claude -> Claude: Extract from:\n- PR title & description\n- Commit messages\n- Code changes\n- Conversation context

Claude -> Claude: Auto-populate fields:\n- Date: 2025-12-02\n- Ticket: FEAT-123\n- Description: "Add feature X"\n- Complexity: Medium\n- Time saved: 2-3 hours

== Documentation Generation ==
Claude -> FS: Read template\n(TEMPLATE.md or TEMPLATE-RESEARCH.md)
activate FS
FS --> Claude: Template content
deactivate FS

Claude -> Claude: Generate complete documentation:\n- TL;DR\n- Objective & Background\n- Technical Details\n- Results & Metrics\n- Lessons Learned

== Save Documentation ==
Claude -> FS: Write documentation to\n.usecase/cases/YYYY-Www-MM-DD_TICKET_description.md
activate FS
FS --> Claude: File created
deactivate FS

== Git Commit ==
Claude -> Git: git add .usecase/cases/[file].md
activate Git
Git --> Claude: Staged
deactivate Git

Claude -> Git: git commit -m "docs: AI session YYYY-MM-DD - TICKET - Description\n\n🤖 Generated with Claude Code\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>"
activate Git
Git --> Claude: Commit created
deactivate Git

== Hub Sync ==
Claude -> CLI: ai-use-case sync
activate CLI
CLI -> DocScript: Execute sync
activate DocScript

DocScript -> FS: Read .usecase/cases/ files
activate FS
FS --> DocScript: Documentation files
deactivate FS

DocScript -> Sync: Invoke sync script
activate Sync

Sync -> Hub: Copy files to by-project/[project]/
activate Hub
Hub --> Sync: Files copied
deactivate Hub

Sync -> Hub: Create symlinks in by-date/YYYY/MM/
activate Hub
Hub --> Sync: Symlinks created
deactivate Hub

Sync -> Hub: Create symlinks in by-topic/[topic]/
activate Hub
Hub --> Sync: Symlinks created
deactivate Hub

Sync -> Git: git add by-project/
activate Git
Git --> Sync: Staged
deactivate Git

Sync -> Git: git commit -m "sync: Add session docs"
activate Git
Git --> Sync: Commit created
deactivate Git

Sync -> Git: git push
activate Git
Git --> Sync: Pushed to remote
deactivate Git

Sync --> DocScript: Sync complete
deactivate Sync
DocScript --> CLI: Success
deactivate DocScript
CLI --> Claude: Documentation synced
deactivate CLI

== Completion ==
Claude -> Developer: ✅ Documentation generated and synced:\n- File: .usecase/cases/[file].md\n- Hub: Synced to by-project/, by-date/, by-topic/\n- Git: Committed and pushed
deactivate Claude

note over Developer, Hub
**Key Features:**
• Automatic version checking
• Interactive session selection (PRs, commits, conversation)
• Parallel git analysis for performance
• Complete documentation (no placeholders)
• Automatic commit and sync to hub
• Support for both implementation and research sessions
end note

@enduml
